        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28256</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28256"/>
        <updated>2025-10-21T07:38:57.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF145 supports the HTTP headers <code class="notranslate">Activate-Storage-Access</code> and <code class="notranslate">Sec-Fetch-Storage-Access</code> in preview in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991688" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1991688</a> (from 145)</p>
<p dir="auto">These are already supported in Chrome 133 - see <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/6146353156849664?gate=5788202676518912" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6146353156849664?gate=5788202676518912</a></p>
<p dir="auto">I don't see a Safari standards position <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2573246463" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/412" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/412/hovercard" href="https://github.com/WebKit/standards-positions/issues/412">WebKit/standards-positions#412</a> so am setting that as false for support.</p>
<p dir="auto">Spec is <a href="https://privacycg.github.io/storage-access-headers" rel="nofollow">https://privacycg.github.io/storage-access-headers</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3510237045" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41499" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41499/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41499">mdn/content#41499</a></p>]]></content>
