        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Chrome 140 Specify GPUTexture in place of GPUTextureView for default views]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28245</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28245"/>
        <updated>2025-10-20T09:37:59.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">In Chrome 140+, there are multiple places in WebGPU methods where a <code class="notranslate">GPUTextureView</code> was expected, but now you can specify a <code class="notranslate">GPUTexture</code> as a shorthand, provided a default <code class="notranslate">GPUTextureView</code> is desired (it is equivalent to a <code class="notranslate">GPUTextureView</code> created using a call to <code class="notranslate">GPUTexture.createView()</code> with no descriptor specified).</p>
<p dir="auto">See <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-140#shorthand_for_using_texture_where_texture_view_is_used" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-140#shorthand_for_using_texture_where_texture_view_is_used</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds data points in the appropriate places.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>

]]></content>
