<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 138 adds the ability for a <code class="notranslate">GPUBuffer</code> to be passed directly into a <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUDevice/createBindGroup" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">GPUDevice.createBindGroup()</code></a> call as a binding resource in place of a <code class="notranslate">GPUBufferBinding</code> object, provided the default <code class="notranslate">size</code> and <code class="notranslate">offset</code> values are being used.</p>
<p dir="auto">See <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#shorthand_for_using_buffer_as_a_binding_resource" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-138#shorthand_for_using_buffer_as_a_binding_resource</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds a data point for the new feature.</p>

